        "AbstractText": "Computational studies on decarboxylative C-H alkenylations provided key insights into the solvent-robust nature of C-H activation/decarboxylation domino reactions. These properties were exploited for ruthenium(II)-catalyzed C-H alkylations by a decarboxylative process with ample scope under copper-free and silver-free reaction conditions."
